        {
          "id": "test-linalg-001",
          "category": "高等代数",
          "sub_category": "行列式×线性方程组",
          "problem": "用 Cramer 法则解方程组 $\\begin{cases}2x+y-z=1\\\\x-y+z=2\\\\x+2y+z=4\\end{cases}$。",
          "solution": "系数行列式 $D=\\begin{vmatrix}2&1&-1\\\\1&-1&1\\\\1&2&1\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot(-1-2)-1\\cdot(1-1)+(-1)\\cdot(2+1)=-6-0-3=-9$。$D_x=\\begin{vmatrix}1&1&-1\\\\2&-1&1\\\\4&2&1\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot(-1-2)-1\\cdot(2-4)+(-1)\\cdot(4+4)=-3+2-8=-9$，$x=\\dfrac{D_x}{D}=\\dfrac{-9}{-9}=1$。$D_y=\\begin{vmatrix}2&1&-1\\\\1&2&1\\\\1&4&1\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot(2-4)-1\\cdot(1-1)+(-1)\\cdot(4-2)=-4-0-2=-6$，$y=\\dfrac{-6}{-9}=\\dfrac{2}{3}$。$D_z=\\begin{vmatrix}2&1&1\\\\1&-1&2\\\\1&2&4\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot(-4-4)-1\\cdot(4-2)+1\\cdot(2+1)=-16-2+3=-15$，$z=\\dfrac{-15}{-9}=\\dfrac{5}{3}$。验证：$2\\cdot 1+\\dfrac{2}{3}-\\dfrac{5}{3}=1$；$1-\\dfrac{2}{3}+\\dfrac{5}{3}=2$；$1+\\dfrac{4}{3}+\\dfrac{5}{3}=4$。",
          "answer": "$(x,y,z)=\\left(1,\\dfrac{2}{3},\\dfrac{5}{3}\\right)$",
